  "narrative": "Estimates are signed to the claimed direction, so a positive signed estimate supports the claim and a negative signed estimate indicates the opposite raw association. H14, H15, H16, H17, H26, and H27 are strong conditional robustness results: SMARCA4 loss remains associated with substantially stronger dependency in TP53-wildtype, matched-omics/CRISPR-QC, and Avana-library samples; TP53 loss remains associated with substantially weaker dependency in SMARCA4-wildtype, matched-omics/CRISPR-QC, and Avana-library samples. These conditional associations persist when excluding co-occurring SMARCA4 or TP53 status and when restricting data-quality or library context, although they remain unadjusted dataset-specific associations rather than causal effects. H24 PTEN loss shows a signed +0.238 association with stronger dependency; the point estimate clearly exceeds the 0.15 threshold and the interval is mostly above the threshold, though the lower bound is marginally below it. Given multiplicity and threshold uncertainty, I accept PTEN as a dataset-specific association but keep it active for conditional robustness and later validation. H22 KEAP1 loss strongly contradicts the original stronger-dependency claim: signed -0.810 indicates a large opposite association, implying weaker dependency in the KEAP1-loss group. I reject the original claim and register a reversed KEAP1 hypothesis for weaker dependency plus a co-occurrence-restricted follow-up. ARID1A, MTAP, and RB1 overall tests are null, small, or not above threshold, so they are rejected and closed. CDKN2A remains borderline: TP53-wildtype follow-up is signed +0.125, below threshold with interval straddling the threshold, so it remains unresolved and deferred. I request independent validation for H13 because it is a large accepted dataset-specific TP53 weaker-dependency claim that remains unvalidated and was explicitly flagged as high priority once conditional robustness remained consistent.",
  "research_notes": "Current dataset-specific accepted findings: H3 SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger dependency, discovery and independent validation. H13 TP53 loss associated with weaker dependency, strong discovery evidence and robust conditional estimates; independent validation now requested. New robustness claims H14, H15, H16, H17, H26, H27 accepted as conditional evidence that SMARCA4 and TP53 associations are not simply explained by excluding the other major predictor, matched-omics/CRISPR-QC restriction, or Avana-library restriction. H24 PTEN loss accepted as a moderate dataset-specific stronger-dependency association, but borderline because the two-sided 95% lower bound is just below 0.15; keep active and registered conditionals within TP53-wildtype, QC, and Avana. H22 KEAP1 original stronger-dependency claim rejected because evidence strongly points to the opposite direction; registered reversed KEAP1 weaker-dependency claims. H4 CDKN2A and H20 CDKN2A-in-TP53-wildtype remain unresolved and deferred. Negative/closed main effects: ARID1A, MTAP, RB1; prior negatives: STK11, KRAS, MYC, research markers, initial interactions. Next priorities: assess H13 validation, then analyze screen-quality claims H28/H29, co-occurrence interactions H30/H31, registered KEAP1 reversals, PTEN conditional robustness, and other untested registered probes. Maintain dataset-specific interpretation; no causal or generalizable mechanistic claim.",
