  "narrative": "All returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For dependency_composite, acceptance requires a signed effect above 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction with uncertainty supporting a threshold-level effect. H37, the main MSI-high association, now has its scheduled independent validation response. Discovery R73 was signed +0.774 with interval +0.664 to +0.885, and validation R78 is signed +0.866 with independent interval +0.693 to +1.040 and valid cells 122 exposed MSI-high versus 1878 comparators. Because H37 direction is -1, positive signed estimates correspond to raw lower composite dependency scores in MSI-high samples, i.e. stronger measured dependency. Both estimates are far above the 0.15 threshold and the validation lower bound is well above threshold, so I accept H37 and close it. H2, STK11 loss, also has a scheduled validation response. Discovery R2 was signed +0.035 with interval -0.040 to +0.111, and validation R79 is signed +0.062 with interval -0.052 to +0.176 and valid cells 360 versus 1640. The validation point estimate is below threshold and the interval is not compatible with a threshold-level effect in the claimed direction. Together with the null discovery result, this provides no support for STK11 loss association, so I reject H2 and close it. H87, PTEN loss restricted to TP53-intact samples on Avana library with screen_roc_auc >= 0.95, received discovery R54 signed +0.195 with interval +0.068 to +0.323, but independent validation R105 is signed +0.085 with interval -0.101 to +0.271 and valid cells 116 versus 714. The discovery was suggestive, but the validation point estimate is below threshold and the interval includes null. The high-quality stratum therefore does not support a threshold-level PTEN effect, and I reject this exact H87 claim and close it. This rejection is specific to the narrow high-quality TP53-intact Avana/ROC stratum; the broader PTEN signal remains borderline and unresolved, but it should not be further mined by additional strata.  Final scientific synthesis: the supported dataset-specific associations are SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger dependency, TP53 loss associated with weaker dependency, KEAP1 loss associated with weaker dependency, and MSI-high associated with stronger dependency. These findings are internally consistent across discovery, validation, and multiple robustness contexts, including TP53-intact or SMARCA4-intact subsets, matched omics/CRISPR QC subsets, Avana library subsets, high screen quality, high or low mutation burden, and the dominant adenocarcinoma subtype. The four mature associations use the same sign in each relevant accepted claim and are well above the 0.15-unit threshold. For SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high, direction -1 claims indicate raw lower dependency scores, i.e. stronger dependency. For TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss, direction +1 claims indicate raw higher dependency scores, i.e. weaker dependency. These are associations in this supplied dataset only and do not establish causal mechanism or biological generalizability.  The broad negative or near-null set includes STK11 loss after validation, KRAS mutation, MYC amplification, ARID1A loss, MTAP loss, RB1 loss, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, PIK3CA mutation, APC mutation, SMAD4 loss, NF1 loss, BRCA2 loss, research markers D/E/F, several technical or culture variables, and tested context amplification interactions by screen quality, mutation burden, EMT score, hypoxia, stemness, TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1 mutual interactions, high Cas9 activity, and upper-half AXL expression. The high-AXL MSI-high result R104 was signed -0.179, opposite the registered amplification direction, suggesting possible attenuation of the MSI-high effect in high-AXL samples. Because that was not the pre-specified claim direction and the interval crossed null, it remains an unresolved post hoc signal only and is not accepted.  Unresolved uncertainty remains mainly for PTEN and CDKN2A. PTEN main effect R22 was signed +0.239 with lower bound +0.145, just below threshold, and validation-like support in TP53-intact samples was not enough for acceptance. H87 validation failure reduces confidence in the narrow high-quality PTEN stratum, but broader PTEN remains borderline and is not an accepted finding. CDKN2A main effect R4 was signed +0.139 with upper bound +0.213, below threshold in point estimate and thus not accepted. The exact-numeric continuous main-effect comparisons H114-H117 were technical invalid cells and do not support or contradict anything.  The most informative next analysis is not more PTEN stratum mining. I activate the already registered high-MYC interactions H120-H123 to test whether expression of MYC, a lineage/proliferation-associated state marker, modifies the accepted predictor associations. I also register four high-IFN-gamma signature interactions for SMARCA4 loss, TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, and MSI-high using a median-like threshold of ifn_gamma_signature >= 0.0. The highest-priority of these is MSI-high among high IFN-gamma samples, because immune signaling may biologically correlate with MSI-associated dependency in this dataset, but the test remains exploratory and dataset-specific. If future discovery evidence shows a threshold-supported interaction, independent validation should be requested before accepting context dependence."
