respond to raw higher dependency scores. Evidence includes R1/R26, TP53-intact-restricted SMARCA4 loss complement R15, QC subset R17, Avana subset R25, high screen-quality subset R38, and adenocarcinoma subset R94. The effect is approximately 0.82-0.84 units. 3) KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker dependency. Accepted direction +1 evidence includes main R20/R39, TP53-intact R31, QC R27, Avana R28, high screen-quality R29, non-Avana R30, and adenocarcinoma R95. The effect is approximately 0.78-0.88 units. 4) MSI-high is associated with stronger dependency. Accepted direction -1 evidence includes main R73/R78, lower mutation burden R80/R92, higher mutation burden R81, TP53-intact R82, high screen-quality R83, and adenocarcinoma R96. The effect is approximately 0.71-0.87 units. The accepted findings are internally consistent across many robustness strata and do not depend on a single technical subgroup.\n\nNegative or null findings. STK11 loss was not supported after validation: discovery R2 was null and validation R79 was signed +0.062 with interval crossing null and below threshold. No meaningful main association was found for KRAS mutation, MYC amplification, ARID1A loss, MTAP loss, RB1 loss, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, PIK3CA mutation, APC mutation, SMAD4 loss, NF1 loss, BRCA2 loss, research markers D/E/F, sex, media-serum contrast 10 versus 5, or the tested technical/QC main contrasts. Context amplification interaction screens were consistently null or below threshold for lineage subtype, research signature A, research signature C, mutual TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1 interactions, screen quality, mutation burden, aneuploidy, EMT, hypoxia, stemness, Cas9 activity, high MYC expression, high IFN-gamma signature, and high growth-rate doublings per day. A few opposite-direction or near-threshold interaction signals, such as TP53 high MYC expression signed +0.128, SMARCA4 high growth rate signed -0.127, and MSI-high high AXL signed -0.179, are not accepted because they are below threshold, interval-crossing, or not in the registered amplification direction. They are post hoc signals only, not context-dependence claims.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. PTEN remains borderline and not accepted: main effect signed +0.239 has lower bound +0.145, just below threshold; TP53-intact discovery and validation are supportive but the latter lower bound is +0.113, below threshold; the narrow high-quality TP53-intact Avana/high-ROC stratum failed validation. CDKN2A also remains unresolved and not accepted: main signed +0.139 is below threshold, and strata are generally below threshold. Exact numeric continuous main-effect comparisons were technically invalid because cells fell below minimum cell-size requirements, so they provide neither support nor contradiction. PTEN and CDKN2A should not be further mined by additional strata unless a new threshold-supported signal emerges.\n\nMost informative next analysis. Externally, the highest-value next step would be independent replication of the four mature associations: SMARCA4 loss toward stronger dependency, TP53 loss toward weaker dependency, KEAP1 loss toward weaker dependency, and MSI-high toward stronger dependency. Within this dataset, the best focused follow-up is not more PTEN or CDKN2A stratum mining and not chasing the weak opposite-direction interaction signals. I registered four pre-specified interaction screens testing whether an above-baseline copy_number_8q24 state, copy_number_8q24 >= 0.0, amplifies the four accepted associations. Each claim uses the same direction as the accepted main association for that predictor, so a positive signed estimate above 0.15 would support amplification in the high-copy-number state relative to its complement. If all are null or below threshold, this will further support robustness of the mature associations. If a threshold-level opposite-direction signal appears, it should not be accepted as attenuation unless a separate confirmatory attenuation hypothesis and validation support it. No new validation is needed at this synthesis step because H106 now has independent validation and no new discovery claim yet requires validation.",
