  "narrative": "The new evidence supports persistence of the four mature associations in reciprocal mature-mutant contexts and in the largest named screen batch. H176 SMARCA4 loss among TP53-loss cells gives signed estimate +0.763 (95% CI +0.653 to +0.873), H177 TP53 loss among SMARCA4-loss cells +0.897 (+0.789 to +1.005), H178 KEAP1 loss among SMARCA4-loss cells +0.790 (+0.661 to +0.920), H179 TP53 loss among KEAP1-loss cells +0.878 (+0.773 to +0.982), and H180 SMARCA4 loss among KEAP1-loss cells +0.814 (+0.684 to +0.945). All are far above the 0.15 composite-unit threshold in the claimed direction, with lower bounds well above threshold. I therefore accept and close H176-H180 as dataset-specific conditional main effects showing that the mature predictors remain associated with dependency_composite when cells already carry another mature alteration. These are persistence/additivity tests, not evidence of effect modification; earlier 2x2 interaction tests did not support multiplicative or context-reversing behavior.\n\nWithin screen_batch batch_a, all four mature effects are also large: H181 SMARCA4 +0.838 (+0.716 to +0.959), H182 TP53 +0.827 (+0.710 to +0.945), H183 KEAP1 +0.731 (+0.595 to +0.866), and H184 MSI-high +0.798 (+0.594 to +1.003). I accept H181-H184 as dataset-specific batch_a main effects. H184 is the least precise because MSI-high is rare, but even there the lower bound is far above the practical threshold. These results reduce concern that the mature associations are generated mainly by a particular assay batch.\n\nThe batch-interaction comparisons do not support effect modification. H185 SMARCA4-by-batch is +0.046 (-0.096 to +0.187), H186 TP53-by-batch is -0.003 (-0.141 to +0.136), and H187 KEAP1-by-batch is -0.107 (-0.262 to +0.047). All are near null relative to the threshold and fail to provide robust threshold-supported evidence of claimed-direction batch modification. I reject H185-H187 and close their investigations. Given repeated null context screens and multiple comparisons, I do not interpret the upper tail of H185 as meaningful. H188 MSI-high-by-batch has no valid result and is closed unresolved to avoid further low-power context mining. I did not request validation because the four mature marginal associations have already been independently validated, and these new conditional/batch effects were expected, large, and have lower bounds far above threshold. Validation budget is better reserved for external orthogonal replication or perturbation experiments if available.",
  "research_notes": "Mature-predictor robustness is now broadly complete. SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high remain associated with stronger dependency, while TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss remain associated with weaker dependency. The associations persist in quality-controlled subsets, mature-mutant-absent subsets, reciprocal mature-mutant contexts, and screen_batch batch_a. Reciprocal mature-mutant main effects H176-H180 were accepted. Batch_a main effects H181-H184 were accepted, including MSI-high with caution due rarity. Batch interactions for SMARCA4, TP53, and KEAP1 were rejected; MSI-high batch interaction H188 closed unresolved. PTEN and CDKN2A remain borderline/unresolved and should not be promoted. No reliable effect modification or context-specific reversal emerged across technical, genomic, lineage, media, omics-availability, or batch screens. Further internal subgroup mining is not likely to add much. The most valuable future evidence is external orthogonal replication and ideally perturbation/rescue experiments for SMARCA4, TP53, KEAP1, and MSI status. All conclusions are dataset-specific measured associations, not causal mechanisms or generalizable clinical claims."
