dia-serum, sex, and broad context interactions do not reliably produce threshold-level effect modification. In particular, the MSI-high by adherent-culture interaction failed validation, and CDKN2A-by-TP53 loss is near null. Unresolved uncertainty: CDKN2A loss remains borderline and unresolved; isolated CDKN2A loss in mature-mutant-abscent cells gave signed +0.168 but lower bound +0.100, below the threshold. Marginal and partially restricted PTEN estimates also remain inconsistent for general acceptance, with some validations below threshold. These remain unresolved and are not promoted. The most informative next internal analyses are the already registered H199 and H200 tests, which examine PTEN loss without CDKN2A loss and CDKN2A loss without PTEN loss inside the mature-mutant-absent population, respectively; they are intended to clarify whether the borderline CDKN2A signal is robust independently of PTEN and whether the newly accepted conditional PTEN signal persists when CDKN2A loss is excluded. Beyond this, the most informative next step is orthogonal external replication and perturbation/rescue testing, not further subgroup mining, because the current conclusions are dataset-specific associations and do not establish causality, mechanism, or generalizability.",
