  "narrative": "Final internal evidence supports five measured dataset-specific predictors with dependency_composite effects exceeding 0.15 units, but only four are broadly validated and one is context restricted. SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger dependency: discovery R3 signed +0.804 [0.742,0.867] and independent validation R13 +0.835 [0.743,0.927], and it remains robust across TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, MSI-high, PTEN-loss, QC, Avana/non-Avana, screen-quality, aneuploidy, and batch contexts. TP53 loss is associated with weaker dependency: discovery R1 +0.829 [0.767,0.891] and validation R26 +0.843 [0.747,0.939], with robust main effects and no supported effect modification. KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker dependency: discovery R20 +0.810 [0.745,0.875] and validation R39 +0.778 [0.685,0.871], robust across reciprocal and mature contexts, with unsupported interactions by library, screen quality, aneuploidy, media, and culture. MSI-high is associated with stronger dependency: discovery R73 +0.775 [0.664,0.885] and validation R78 +0.866 [0.693,1.040]; it is rare but remains above threshold in mature, low-quality-screen, and mature-mutant-absent contexts, while interaction claims by culture and batch are unsupported. PTEN loss is not supported unconditionally. The supported PTEN claim is H192, restricted to TP53-WT/KEAP1-WT/MSI-negative cells: discovery R181 +0.286 [0.196,0.376] and validation R190 +0.311 [0.178,0.444], so I accept H192 at response deadline. The adenocarcinoma-subset refinement H207 was supported by discovery R204 +0.271 [0.168,0.374], but independent validation R216 gives +0.251 [0.107,0.394]; the adjusted lower bound falls below 0.15, so I downgrade H207 to unresolved and close the exact subset claim. This does not contradict H192; it indicates that the adenocarcinoma-specific magnitude is not independently confirmed at the threshold level. Negative or non-supporting findings include STK11 loss after validation, all constructed research markers D/E/F, ARID1A, MTAP, KRAS, MYC amplification, PIK3CA, EGFR, ERBB2, APC, SMAD4, NF1, BRAF, BRCA2, and most technical covariates such as media serum, library, omics availability, sex, batch interactions, culture interactions, and lineage interactions for SMARCA4/TP53/KEAP1/MSI. CDKN2A loss remains borderline: point estimates often exceed 0.15, but discovery lower bounds generally remain below threshold and interactions are null, so it is not accepted. The CDKN2A-WT PTEN restriction H199 and stringent triple-restricted PTEN H87 are unresolved or rejected. All statements are associations measured in the supplied dataset; none establishes causality, mechanism, biological interpretation, or generalizability. The most informative next internal analysis is the new PTEN-by-adenocarcinoma interaction within the mature-mutant-absent eligible population, plus the already active H215 low-screen-quality PTEN test. The interaction will determine whether H207 validation shortfall reflects lineage heterogeneity or sampling/power: a threshold-sized positive signed interaction would support enhanced PTEN dependency in adenocarcinoma, a near-null interaction would favor power and retain the broad H192 PTEN association, and a threshold-sized negative signed interaction would motivate a separate attenuation claim. External replication and perturbation/rescue in the mature-mutant-absent PTEN context are the strongest later steps for generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Updated internal synthesis. Supported dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency (validated; lower bounds exceed 0.15; robust across QC, mature contexts, batch, screen quality, library, and reciprocal mutation contexts). TP53 loss weaker dependency (validated; robust). KEAP1 loss weaker dependency (validated; robust). MSI-high stronger dependency (validated; robust though rare; lineage/technical interactions unsupported). PTEN loss supported only within TP53-WT/KEAP1-WT/MSI-negative mature cells (H192: discovery +0.286 lower +0.196; validation +0.311 lower +0.178). Unconditional PTEN and stricter PTEN contexts are unresolved or rejected. H207 adenocarcinoma-subset PTEN was accepted on discovery (+0.271 lower +0.168), but validation (+0.251 lower +0.107) did not clear the 0.15-unit threshold, so the exact adenocarcinoma-subset claim is unresolved and closed. H199 CDKN2A-WT PTEN restriction remains unresolved for the analogous reason. CDKN2A loss remains borderline and is not accepted. STK11, constructed markers D/E/F, ARID1A, MTAP, many common driver alterations, technical covariates, and most interactions are null or unsupported. No causal, mechanistic, biological-pathway, or generalizable claims are supported. No validation slots remain. Next analyze stage should test H215 (PTEN loss in mature-mutant-absent cells with screen_roc_auc <= 0.95) and the newly registered PTEN-by-adenocarcinoma interaction within the mature-mutant-absent population to resolve whether H207's validation shortfall reflects power or lineage heterogeneity. If that interaction is near null and broad mature PTEN validation remains strong, retain H192 as the primary PTEN association and avoid further subgroup mining. External replication and perturbation/rescue are needed for generalizability."
