  "narrative": "Final synthesis. The due validation deadline concerns H199, PTEN-loss dependency contrast among TP53-loss-negative, KEAP1-loss-negative, MSI-negative, CDKN2A-loss-negative cells. Discovery evidence R191 gave a signed PTEN-loss estimate of +0.273 [0.177,0.370], which exceeded the 0.15-unit threshold. The independent validation R203 gave +0.243 [0.091,0.395]; the point estimate is clearly positive, but the adjusted lower bound is below the threshold. I therefore keep H199 unresolved and closed: this most restricted PTEN context is compatible with the broader PTEN finding but is not independently threshold-supported. This is not evidence against the accepted mature-context PTEN association; it means the CDKN2A-WT restriction does not, by itself, clear the adjusted evidentiary bar in the supplied data.\n\nSupported dataset-specific findings. SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger dependency: discovery R3 +0.804 [0.742,0.867] and independent validation R13 +0.835 [0.743,0.927], with robustness across reciprocal-mutant, QC, library, screen-quality, aneuploidy, lineage, batch, and mature-mutant-absent strata. TP53 loss is associated with weaker dependency, i.e. higher/less negative dependency scores: R1 +0.829 [0.767,0.891] and validation R26 +0.843 [0.747,0.939], with no supported effect modification by major subgroup tests. KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker dependency: R20 +0.810 [0.745,0.875] and validation R39 +0.778 [0.685,0.871], robust across contexts and with unsupported interactions by library, screen quality, aneuploidy, media, culture, and co-mutational status. MSI-high is associated with stronger dependency: R73 +0.775 [0.664,0.885] and validation R78 +0.866 [0.693,1.040], although MSI-high is rare; it remains threshold-positive in many mature and restricted contexts, while its interaction claims are not supported. PTEN loss is not accepted unconditionally. The supported PTEN association is the mature TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative context H192: R181 +0.286 [0.196,0.376] and validation R190 +0.311 [0.178,0.444]. The lower-screen-quality stratum R217 +0.336 [0.194,0.479] supports this context effect, and the high-screen-quality stratum R221 +0.238 [0.122,0.354] is consistent but not independently threshold-supported. The adenocarcinoma-subset PTEN claim remains uncertain because R204 +0.271 [0.168,0.374] was followed by independent validation R216 +0.251 [0.107,0.394], with lower bound below threshold; the PTEN-by-adenocarcinoma interaction R218 -0.052 [-0.265,0.162] does not support lineage modification, so the adenocarcinoma-subset shortfall is more consistent with power/threshold uncertainty than supported attenuation.\n\nNegative or non-supporting findings. STK11 loss is not supported for stronger dependency: direction-consistent discovery and validation remain null, including R2 +0.035 [-0.040,0.111] and R79 +0.062 [-0.052,0.177]. Constructed markers D, E, and F show no meaningful main effects: R7, R8, and R9 are centered near zero. Common mutational predictors do not clear the threshold: ARID1A, MTAP, KRAS, MYC amplification, PIK3CA, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, APC, SMAD4, NF1, BRAF, and BRCA2 are unsupported after main-effect and interaction/context tests. Technical and demographic covariates are also unsupported as broad predictors, including media serum, CRISPR library indicators, omics availability, matched-RNA-DNA-CRISPR QC, and sex. Interaction mining did not identify supported effect modification of the main SMARCA4, TP53, KEAP1, or MSI-high associations. PTEN-by-CDKN2A interaction R222 +0.061 [-0.183,0.304] is unsupported, and PTEN-by-high-aneuploidy R197 -0.162 [-0.361,0.037] is not supported.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. CDKN2A loss remains a borderline unresolved signal rather than a supported scientific finding. Many CDKN2A point estimates are positive and in the stronger-dependency direction, but intervals usually include effects below 0.15 or cell-count constraints make tests inconclusive: H4 R4 +0.139 [0.065,0.213], H20/H203/H204/H218 are borderline or restricted, and the stringent interaction H217 is invalid due insufficient cells in one comparison cell. Therefore CDKN2A should not be reported as a threshold-exceeding predictor. PTEN also remains contextually uncertain: H199 unresolved as above; H87 strict TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative Avana/high-screen-quality PTEN claim is rejected because independent validation R105 +0.085 [-0.101,0.271] did not support the threshold. These limitations are precision/context limitations, not evidence of causality or biological interpretation.\n\nConclusion and next investigation. The best-supported conclusion from this dataset is that SMARCA4 loss, TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, MSI-high, and PTEN loss only in a mature TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative context are associated with scientifically meaningful differences in the composite dependency score, with all effects interpreted as measured associations in the supplied dataset. The next most informative analysis would not be additional broad subgroup mining, which risks false-positive selection. If new evidence becomes available, the priority would be a pre-specified independent replication of (1) the PTEN-loss contrast in the TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative mature context, especially the CDKN2A-WT and high-screen-quality strata, and (2) the CDKN2A-loss context test, particularly the low-9p21 mature-mutant-absent strata. Within this run, validation slots are exhausted and discovery evidence is already mature for the central findings; further internal analyses are not informative enough to justify changing the conclusions.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis after H199 response deadline. H199 kept unresolved/closed: discovery R191 +0.273 [0.177,0.370] exceeds threshold, but independent validation R203 +0.243 [0.091,0.395] has adjusted lower bound below threshold; CDKN2A-WT restricted PTEN context is compatible with, but not independently threshold-supported by, the broader PTEN finding. Accepted/supported dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency (R3/R13 and robust contexts), TP53 loss weaker dependency (R1/R26), KEAP1 loss weaker dependency (R20/R39), MSI-high stronger dependency (R73/R78), and PTEN loss stronger dependency only in TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative mature context (H192: R181/R190; robust low-screen R217; high-screen R221 supportive but not accepted). PTEN is not accepted unconditionally, as an adenocarcinoma-specific effect (R204/R216 unresolved; H216 interaction rejected), as a CDKN2A-WT effect (H199 unresolved), or under the strictest triple-restricted quality context (H87 rejected via R105). Negative/null findings: STK11 loss (R79), markers D/E/F (R7/R8/R9), ARID1A, MTAP, KRAS, MYC amplification, PIK3CA, EGFR, ERBB2, APC, SMAD4, NF1, BRAF, BRCA2, technical/media/library/omics/sex effects, and interaction tests for the main predictors. CDKN2A remains borderline: point estimates are often positive, but intervals or insufficient cells prevent threshold-supported acceptance; no CDKN2A interaction accepted. No validation slots remain. Final report: dataset-specific associations only; no causal, mechanistic, biological-pathway, or generalizability claims. Future work should pre-specify external replication of the mature-context PTEN loss effect and CDKN2A low-9p21/mature-mutant-absent context rather than further exploratory mining."
}

