  "narrative": "No response deadlines were active, and no additional independent-validation request remains available. The newly relevant PTEN validation evidence does not change the central conclusions but refines the status of conditional PTEN claims. H207 tests PTEN loss versus no PTEN loss in the mature TP53-loss-negative, KEAP1-loss-negative, MSI-negative adenocarcinoma population. The discovery estimate is +0.271 with 95% interval [0.168, 0.374], and the independent adjusted validation estimate is +0.251 with interval [0.107, 0.394]. The direction is consistent and the point estimate is substantively above the 0.15-unit threshold, but the validation lower bound crosses below that threshold. I therefore keep H207 unresolved rather than accept or reject it. H199 has the same pattern: discovery +0.273 [0.177, 0.370] but validation +0.243 [0.091, 0.395], so it remains unresolved. By contrast, H192, PTEN loss in the mature TP53-loss-negative, KEAP1-loss-negative, MSI-negative context without the additional lineage or CDKN2A restrictions, remains supported: discovery +0.286 [0.196, 0.376] and validation +0.311 [0.179, 0.444], both above the scientific-meaning threshold. I therefore retain H192 as accepted.   Supported dataset-specific findings. The clearest robust associations are four measured predictors, all in the claimed direction and robust across many eligibility, technical, and validation checks. First, SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger composite dependency, meaning more negative dependency scores: central evidence H3/R3 is +0.804 [0.742, 0.867], with validation H13/R13 +0.835 [0.743, 0.927], and many conditional or technical-stratum analyses remain above the 0.15-unit threshold. Second, TP53 loss is associated with weaker composite dependency, meaning less negative scores: reversal claim H13/R1 gives +0.829 [0.767, 0.891] and validation R26 gives +0.843 [0.747, 0.939], with robust conditional support. Third, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker composite dependency: reversal claim H38/R20 gives +0.810 [0.745, 0.875] and validation R39 gives +0.778 [0.685, 0.871], again robust across many conditional strata. Fourth, MSI-high is associated with stronger composite dependency despite its lower prevalence: H37/R73 gives +0.775 [0.664, 0.885] and validation R78 gives +0.866 [0.693, 1.040], and the association remains large within mutation-burden, TP53, screen-quality, co-loss, and other pre-specified contexts. Fifth, PTEN loss is not a uniformly accepted broad predictor, but it is supported in a defined mature molecular context: TP53-loss-negative, KEAP1-loss-negative, MSI-negative. H192/R181 gives +0.286 [0.196, 0.376] with validation R190 +0.311 [0.179, 0.444]; other mature-context robustness checks are directionally consistent. This is a dataset-specific conditional association, not evidence that PTEN loss causes dependency or that the effect generalizes beyond the tested population.   Negative and non-supporting findings. Several predictors do not show scientifically meaningful differences: STK11 loss, constructed markers D/E/F, and most common mutational predictors including EGFR, ERBB2, PIK3CA, APC, SMAD4, NF1, BRAF, BRCA2, MYC amplification, KRAS, ARID1A, MTAP, RB1, and related broad effects are not threshold-supported in the tested directions. Technical and demographic covariates also do not show meaningful direct dependency differences, including sex, CRISPR library, omics availability, screen QC availability, media serum concentration comparisons, and screen batch effects not central to the primary predictors. Interaction analyses generally failed to support effect modification for the central predictors across lineage subtype, aneuploidy, ploidy, mutation burden, EMT, hypoxia, growth rate, IFN-gamma, MYC/AXL/SLFN11 expression proxies, research signatures, culture type, sex, media, and screen quality or library strata. Notably, H152 appeared promising in discovery but failed independent validation, and all newly assessed research_signature_b interactions are unsupported. These are non-supporting findings, not proofs of exact absence.   Unresolved uncertainty. The main unresolved area is PTEN loss in narrower conditional strata and CDKN2A loss. Broad PTEN, H24/R22, is near threshold but not robustly supported, with discovery +0.239 and validation patterns that include lower bounds below 0.15 when conditioning more narrowly. Several mature or quality-stratified PTEN claims remain unresolved, including H199, H207, H219, H221, and H228, because the point estimates are often meaningful but the independent or subgroup lower bounds fall below threshold or no further validation is possible. CDKN2A loss is similarly borderline: estimates are frequently in the stronger-dependency direction but lower bounds are below the 0.15-unit threshold, so it remains unresolved and is not accepted as a central predictor. These unresolved items are precision or context limitations, not evidence of opposite direction.   Most informative next analysis. If external replication becomes available, the highest-value follow-up is a small set of pre-specified independent tests: PTEN loss in the mature TP53/KEAP1/MSI-negative context, especially stringent CDKN2A-negative or high-screen-quality strata; and CDKN2A loss in mature, low-9p21, high-quality contexts. Further broad subgroup mining in this dataset is not justified because it increases selection artifacts and cannot repair independent-validation shortfall. All conclusions in this report are measured associations within the supplied composite dependency-score dataset. They do not establish causality, mechanism, single-gene knockout effects, or generalizability to other populations or experimental systems.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis. No validation requests remain and no proposals are registered to avoid post-hoc subgroup mining. Accepted robust dataset-specific associations: SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency; TP53 loss weaker dependency; KEAP1 loss weaker dependency; MSI-high stronger dependency; PTEN loss stronger dependency in mature TP53-loss/KEAP1-loss/MSI-negative context with accepted validation for H192. Negative or unsupported: STK11, constructed markers D/E/F, most common mutational predictors, broad technical/demographic covariates, and most interaction claims. Unresolved: PTEN in narrower mature/adenocarcinoma/CDKN2A-negative/high-quality strata and CDKN2A as a borderline central predictor. H207 and H199 remain unresolved because validation direction is consistent but adjusted lower bounds fall below the 0.15-unit threshold. Next best analysis would be independent pre-specified replication of PTEN mature-context and CDKN2A stringent-context claims; no further exploration of this dataset is warranted. All claims are associations in supplied data, not causal or generalizable conclusions."
